Build fixes for Hyprland 0.56.2 on OHOS musl (clang23 + libc++_ohm), on top of
D's hyprland-0.56.2-hongmeng.patch. All are target/portability fixes:

1) src/xwayland/XWM.cpp: the <xcb/*> includes sat before the `#ifndef NO_XWAYLAND`
   guard, so a NO_XWAYLAND build (no xcb/X11 in the sysroot) failed. Move them inside.

--- a/src/xwayland/XWM.cpp
+++ b/src/xwayland/XWM.cpp
@@ -2,9 +2,9 @@
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <memory>
 #include <string>
-#include <xcb/xfixes.h>
-#include <xcb/xproto.h>
 #ifndef NO_XWAYLAND
+#include <xcb/xfixes.h>
+#include <xcb/xproto.h>
 
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <cstring>

2) scripts/generateShaderIncludes.sh: `echo -n 'R"#('` writes a literal "-n " under a
   POSIX /bin/sh whose echo lacks -n (macOS); the shader .inc then won't compile. Use
   printf 'R"#(' instead.

3) macOS build host only: Hyprland's generated protocol wrappers (protocols/foo.hpp) and
   hand-written implementations (src/protocols/Foo.hpp) collide on a case-insensitive
   filesystem, as does the `VERSION` file with libc++'s <version>. Build on a
   case-sensitive volume (hdiutil create -fs "Case-sensitive APFS"). No source change
   needed there. (On a case-sensitive Linux host none of this applies.)

4) The dma-buf sync-file ioctls (DMA_BUF_IOCTL_EXPORT_SYNC_FILE) that src/helpers/Drm.cpp
   uses are absent from OHOS kernel uapi; provided via device/userspace/uapi-fix/linux/dma-buf.h.
